Inline marks `marks(s)` of a source line build a new text walking s with an italic flag starting off. A "`" starts a code span: append byte 1, copy bytes unchanged up to the next "`", append byte 1 for it and continue after it (an unclosed span runs to the end). A backslash followed by one of the bytes "\", "`", "*", "_", "~", "$", "[", "]", "(", ")", "#", "|" appends that byte and skips both. "**" or "__" appends byte 2 and skips both; "~~" appends byte 4. A single "*" toggles italic (append byte 3) when italic is off and the next byte exists and is not a space, or when italic is on and the previous byte is not a space; a single "_" does the same but only when, opening, the previous byte is missing or not a letter or digit, and, closing, the next byte is missing or not a letter or digit, so snake_case names stay intact; otherwise they are copied. Math: "$$" looks for the next "$$" after it; a single "$" counts only when the next byte is not a space and then looks for the next "$" whose previous byte is not a space and whose next byte is missing or not a digit; "\(" looks for the next "\)". When the closer is found append byte 5, tex of the text between, byte 5, and continue after the closer; else copy the byte. Links: a "[" with a later "](" and a ")" after that appends byte 6, marks of the text between "[" and "](", byte 6, and continues after the ")"; a "!" right before such a "[" is dropped. Every other byte is copied.

`emit(out, t, base)` adds a whole message t with base kind letter base. Split t on newlines into source lines, with a code flag and a math flag starting off. For each source line s with leading and trailing spaces trimmed into ts: when the code flag is on, a ts starting with "```" turns it off, else wrap s as kind "c" with no inline marks. When the math flag is on, a ts equal to "$$" or "\]" turns it off, else wrap tex(ts) as kind "M". Otherwise a ts starting with "```" turns the code flag on, and a ts equal to "$$" or "\[" turns the math flag on. Otherwise when base is not "p": wrap marks(s) as kind base. Otherwise: an empty ts pushes "p" unless out is empty or out's last line is just "p"; a ts longer than 4 bytes that starts and ends with "$$" wraps tex of the text between as kind "M"; one "#" followed by a space makes kind "h", two make kind "g" and three to six make kind "j", each from marks of the text after that space; a ts of three or more characters, all "-", all "*" or all "_", pushes "r"; a ts starting with "|" whose bytes are all among "|", "-", ":" and space changes out's last line kind byte from "b" to "H" when it is "b" and pushes nothing; any other ts starting with "|" splits ts on "|", drops the first piece and the last piece when empty, trims each piece, applies marks to each and joins them with byte 9 as kind "b"; leading spaces n then "- ", "* " or "+ " and a rest: the rest starting with "[ ] " makes kind "p" from twice n spaces, "☐ " and marks of the rest after those 4 bytes, starting with "[x] " or "[X] " the same with "☑ ", else kind "p" from twice n spaces, the bullet ("•" when n is below 2, "◦" below 4, else "▪"), a space and marks of the rest; leading spaces n then one or more digits then ". " or ") " make kind "p" from twice n spaces, byte 2, the digits, ".", byte 2, a space and marks of the text after; "> " makes kind "q" from marks of the rest; anything else is kind "p" from marks(s).

Fixed decimals of a non-negative real v with d decimals: round v times 10 to the d to an integer, write the integer part, then "." and the remainder zero-padded to d digits (no point when d is 0). Compact count of a non-negative real v: below 1000 the integer of v; below 1000000 fixed 1 decimal of v/1000 followed by "K"; else fixed 2 decimals of v/1000000 followed by "M". Spinner at time t: the frame int(t*8) modulo 10 indexes "·", "✢", "✳", "✶", "✻", "✽", "✻", "✶", "✳", "✢". Tool summary of a JSON node: the first non-empty string member among "file_path", "command", "pattern", "path", "url", "query", "description", "prompt", cut at its first newline, in tilde form, and when longer than 90 bytes cut to 87 bytes (backing up past continuation bytes 128 to 191) plus "…".

Event parsing takes one JSON object node n and the session index i. A string member reads as its text, else "". The id is the first non-empty of "session_id", "sessionID", "conversation_id"; when non-empty it replaces the session id. A number member reads with `json::as_f64`, missing as 0. Thinking text th emits, when its trimmed first line is non-empty, "✻ " + byte 3 + that line (cut to 140 bytes backing up past continuation bytes 128 to 191, plus "…" when cut) + byte 3 as base "k". With type t: "user" with non-empty "text" pushes "p" then emits text as base "u", sets the activity to "Starting", then stops. "user" with a "message" member: the activity becomes "Reading results"; for each element of its "content" with "type" "tool_result" and "is_error" true, the error text is its "content" when a string, else the "text" of the content's first element; emit "Tool failed: " plus its first line as base "e"; then stop. "system": when "cwd" is non-empty store it as the session cwd, when "model" is non-empty store it as the session model, when "permissionMode" is non-empty store it as the permission mode; stop. "assistant" with a "message" member m: when m's "model" is non-empty and the session model is empty store it; when m has a "usage" member u, the sum of u's "input_tokens", "cache_creation_input_tokens", "cache_read_input_tokens" and "output_tokens" becomes the context tokens when above 0; for each element of m's "content": type "thinking" emits its "thinking" as thinking text and sets the activity to "Thinking", type "redacted_thinking" sets the activity to "Thinking", type "text" emits its "text" as base "p" and sets the activity to "Writing", type "tool_use" emits byte 2, its "name", byte 2, two spaces and the tool summary of its "input" member as base "t" and sets the activity to "Running " + its "name"; stop. With a "part" member pt: type "text" emits its text as base "p" and sets the activity to "Writing"; type "reasoning" emits its "text" as thinking text and sets the activity to "Thinking"; type "tool" emits byte 2, its "tool", byte 2, two spaces and the tool summary of the part's "state" member's "input" member as base "t" and sets the activity to "Running " + its "tool"; type "step-finish" with a "tokens" member k: the sum of k's "input", "output", "reasoning" and k's "cache" member's "read" and "write" becomes the context tokens when above 0, the cost grows by pt's "cost" and the output tokens by k's "output"; stop. "result": the activity becomes empty, the cost grows by "total_cost_usd", the turn count by the integer of "num_turns" and the output tokens by the "output_tokens" of its "usage" member; when "is_error" is true and "result" is non-empty emit "result" as base "e"; then build pieces: "done in " plus fixed 1 decimal of "duration_ms" over 1000 plus " s" when that number exists, "$" plus fixed 4 decimals of "total_cost_usd" when it exists, "num_turns" plus " turn" when it is 1 else plus " turns", when it exists; join with "  ·  " and emit as base "m" when any; stop. Types "stream_event", "step_start", "step_finish" stop. Error message: when "error" is a string, that string; else error's "message" if non-empty, else error's "data" "message". Non-empty emits it as base "e" and stops. Otherwise emit the first non-empty of "response", "text", "output" as base "p" if any.

Refreshing session i: busy is whether "dir/busy" exists; when busy and the busy start is negative set it to NOW, when not busy set it to -1. Read "dir/log.jsonl" and "dir/err.log" (missing reads as empty); when log length + 7 * err length equals the stored size do nothing, else store it, set the activity to empty and the context tokens, cost, output tokens and turn count to 0. Split the log on newlines; a line starting with "{" clears the accumulator; append the line and a newline; parse the accumulator into one reused Doc, and on success clear it and parse the event. Then if err is non-empty and not busy, emit each non-empty line among the last three of err split on newlines as base "e". Replace the session's lines and id.

The command for session i in dir d, with rs = flag + id when the id is non-empty (flags " --session ", " --resume ", " --conversation ", " -s " by platform), else empty:
- p1: "claude -p --output-format stream-json --verbose --permission-mode acceptEdits" rs " < 'd/prompt.txt'"
- p2: "agy --print \"$(cat 'd/prompt.txt')\" --output-format json" rs
- p3: "opencode run --format json ${AMNI_DIAL_OPENCODE_MODEL:+-m $AMNI_DIAL_OPENCODE_MODEL}" rs " < 'd/prompt.txt'"
- p0: "grok --prompt-file 'd/prompt.txt' --output-format streaming-messages-json --permission-mode dontAsk" (no rs)

Sending does nothing when INPUT is empty or CUR's platform is unavailable, busy or demo. Otherwise write INPUT to "d/prompt.txt"; append `{"type":"user","text":` + JSON string of INPUT + "}\n" to the log; write "1" to "d/busy", mark busy and set busy start to NOW; write "d/run.sh" as ENVP + command + " >> 'd/log.jsonl' 2>> 'd/err.log'; rm -f 'd/busy'\n"; run `if command -v setsid >/dev/null; then setsid -f sh 'd/run.sh'; else (sh 'd/run.sh' &); fi >/dev/null 2>&1 </dev/null`; clear INPUT, VIEWT = 0, refresh CUR.

Seeding from path: if the file cannot be read print "no transcript " + path and stop. For the first Claude session write its log as `{"type":"user","text":"Make one focused improvement to helium-graphics."}` newline `{"type":"replay","text":` + JSON string of the file + "}\n", write "recorded Claude Code run, replayed" to its "demo" file, set demo and size -1.

Drawing primitives append untextured vertices (uv (-1,-1)). A quad p0 p1 p2 p3 with colors c0 c1 c2 c3 is the triangles p0 p1 p2 and p0 p2 p3 with matching colors; a flat quad uses one color. pt(r, a) = (CX + r*cos(a), CY + r*sin(a)*YS). A band from radius r0 to r1 over angles a0 to a1 with inner color ci and outer color co uses n = max(1, int(|a1-a0|/0.02) + 1) quads with u_k = a0 + (a1-a0)*k/n, corners pt(r0,u0), pt(r1,u0), pt(r1,u1), pt(r0,u1) colored ci, co, co, ci; a one-color band passes the color twice. A disc temporarily moves the center to (x, y) and draws a one-color band 0 to r over 0 to 6.2832. A segment from p to q of width w offsets by n = the unit normal of q - p times w*0.5 and draws the flat quad p-n, q-n, q+n, p+n. A spoke at angle a, radii r0 to r1, width w is the segment from pt(r0,a) to pt(r1,a).

Font metrics, once at startup: lay out "Hgjy|" into a scratch list with `sdf_text(list, 0, 0, 100, "Hgjy|", white, 0, false)` (eight arguments, the last is the outline flag); FY0 is the smallest vertex y over 100 and FY1 the largest over 100. FC is the middle of the smallest and largest vertex y of "H" laid out alone the same way into a second scratch list, over 100 (the capital-letter center). Line height at size s is (FY1 - FY0) * s * 1.12.

Rich text `rich(vs, x, y, size, t, c, weight, cw, draw)` lays out display text t (no kind letter) left to right from pen x and returns the pen advance. Text at (x, y) and size s has its capital letters from y to y + s, so its baseline is y + s. Style flags code, bold, italic, strike, math and link start off and the marker bytes 1 to 6 toggle them in that order; bytes 7 and 8 toggle raised and lowered flags. A raised run uses size*0.7 with its top at y - size*0.15 and a lowered run size*0.7 with its top at y + size*0.5; that run's size and top stand in for size and y in everything it lays out, draws and advances. Runs between marker bytes are laid out with `sdf_text(vs, pen, y, size, run, color, w, false)` (eight arguments, the last is the outline flag) when draw is set, and the pen grows by `sdf_text_w` of the run. A run's color is accent 1 when link, else accent 5 when math, else accent 0 when code, else c, always with c's alpha; when bold it is mixed 35% toward white when dark or toward black when light, alpha kept; w is 1 when bold else weight. Code runs get padding: the pen grows by size*0.18 before and after the run, and when drawing, before the run's text, a pill `sdf_rect(vs, pen - size*0.14, y - size*0.26, run width + size*0.28, size*1.56, accent 0 with alpha c's alpha*0.16)`. When drawing an italic run, every vertex the run emitted (from the list length before it to the end, pill excluded) moves its x by (y + size - its y)*0.2. When drawing, a strike run adds `sdf_rect(vs, run start, y + size*0.58, run width, max(1, size*0.075), run color)` and a link run adds `sdf_rect(vs, run start, y + size*1.14, run width, max(1, size*0.06), run color with alpha times 0.7)`. Byte 9 moves the pen to x + cw times the cell index so far. Vertices that `sdf_text` emits with zero RGB get the shadow color for c's alpha over 255.

Arc text `arctext(vs, t, r, a, size, c, weight, tilt, center, cw)` returns an end angle. Lay out t with rich at origin, drawing. fl is sin(a) above 0.25; w is the returned advance; hw = w*0.5/r; start a0 is a+hw when fl and centered, a-hw when only centered, else a. Each new vertex p maps to q = pt(r - (FY1*size - p.y)*tilt, a0 - p.x/r) when fl, else pt(r - (p.y - FY0*size)*tilt, a0 + p.x/r). When WG is above 0, with d = q - (BX,BY): sw = WG*WG*1.5*(1 + 45/(sqrt(dx*dx+dy*dy)+30)), pl = 1 - pow(WG,1.1)*0.97, position = (BX + (dx*cos(sw) - dy*sin(sw))*pl, BY + (dx*sin(sw) + dy*cos(sw))*pl*(1 - WG*0.5)). The end angle is a0 - w/r when fl, else a0 + w/r. `arc_mid(m, a, size)` is the radius at which arc text at angle a and that size centers its capital letters on radius m: m + (FY1 - FC)*size when sin(a) is above 0.25, else m + (FC - FY0)*size. Flat text `flat(vs, x, y, size, t, c, weight)` is rich at (x, y) with cw 0, drawing, returning the advance.

Logo, once at startup: PNG-decode the embedded "amniscient-logo.png" (skip on failure), ch = bytes/(w*h). Over a 112 grid, each cell averages 4 samples k at pixel offset ((y*h/112 + k%2*4)*w + x*w/112 + k/2*4)*ch: s grows by c*0.25 and lo by (1 - min(r,g,b))*0.25. Alpha = clamp(lo*2.2, 0, 1); skip below 0.05; add a quad of color rgba(s, alpha) from (x/112*2-1, y/112*2-1) with side 2/112.

Status of session i: demo gives "DEMO REPLAY  ·  recorded Claude Code run"; unavailable gives "no public Grok Bot API  ·  install the grok CLI to drive this sector" for p0, else exe + " not installed  ·  adapter ready"; busy gives the spinner at NOW, a space, the activity (or "Working" when empty) and "…", then, when the busy start is not negative, appends `str("  ", int(NOW - busy start), " s")` (never `format`, which would treat "  " as a pattern); else "live  ·  Enter sends". Its tone is accent 5 for demo, 2 unavailable, 4 busy, else 3.

Meters of session i: its context window is 1000000 when its model contains "[1m]" or its platform is 2, else 200000; its context fraction is clamp(context tokens / window, 0, 1). The gauge color for fraction f with alpha a is accent 3 below 0.5, accent 4 below 0.8, else accent 2.

Geometry per draw: a = span*0.5*RAD; S0 = clamp(H*0.024, 13, 27); R = H*1.3 + W*0.5/sin(a); CX = W*0.5; CY = H*0.935 - R. w = W*0.78/S0; when |w - WRAPU| exceeds 0.5, set WRAPU = w and reset size to -1 and refresh every session. Text size at radius r is S0*exp(-(R-r)/(H*1.7)). The hole depth is H*0.78 and the hole radius H*0.047.

GPU setup `gpu()`: the first time, PB = a pipeline of embedded shaders "shaders/screen.vert" and "shaders/hole.frag" with the default description; PO the same shaders with blend `gfx::BLEND_PREMULTIPLIED`; PD = "shaders/screen.vert" with "shaders/post.frag" default; PU the same with blend `gfx::BLEND_ADD`; SM = a linear clamped sampler; READY true. Then when TW differs from W or TH from H: release SC and the four BL textures if TW is above 0, make SC a W by H `gfx::RGBA16F` render target and BL[k] a max(1, W >> (k+1)) by max(1, H >> (k+1)) RGBA16F render target, set TW = W, TH = H.

A hole pass with mode m (0 backdrop, 1 overlay) opens a render pass with `gfx::begin_pass(gfx::PassDesc { color: [SC, gfx::Texture { 0 }, gfx::Texture { 0 }, gfx::Texture { 0 }], clear_color: c, .. })` where c is whether the mode is 0 (the field is `clear_color`; cleared passes clear to black), binds PB for mode 0 or PO for mode 1, sets fragment uniforms slot 0 to `HoleU` with a = (W, H, NOW modulo 1000, 0 when DARK else 1), h0 and h1 the first and second holes (zeros when absent), m = (mode, 0.27, 1, 0), draws 3 vertices and ends the pass. A post pass into dst from src and glo with mode m, strength k and add flag opens the same kind of pass on dst with `clear_color` set unless add, binds PU when add else PD, binds fragment textures slot 0 src and slot 1 glo with SM, sets fragment uniforms slot 0 to `PostU` with a = (1/src width, 1/src height, m, k) and b = (NOW modulo 1000, 0.78, 0.022 when DARK else 0, 0 when DARK else 1), draws 3 vertices and ends the pass. Texture sizes come from `gfx::texture_info`.

Adding a hole (x, y, radius, alpha): when NH is below 2 store it and count it; otherwise replace the stored hole of lower alpha when alpha is higher.

Crawl for session i at angle c with alpha a writes lines into va and the prompt into vb. hh = H; r0 = R - S0*1.75; n = visible(i); me is 1 for CUR else 0; the hole center is pt(R - hh*0.78, c) into BX, BY, added as a hole with radius hh*0.047 and alpha a. rr = r0 - S0*2.3 + (SCROLL + VIEWF - VIEW)*line height(S0)*me, so whole-line scrolling moves smoothly by the eased fraction. bw is WRAPU*S0*0.5 and the left edge angle L = c + bw*0.9/r0 (at the bottom of the screen larger angles are further left). For k from 0 while k is below 240 and the line index n-1-VIEW*me-k is at least 0: l is that line, kd its kind letter, x its text after the kind byte. f = (R-rr)/(hh*0.78), stop if above 1. size = size(rr) times 1.32 for "h", 1.16 for "g", 1.04 for "j", 1.1 for "M", 0.92 for "k", 0.87 for "m", else 1. WG = clamp((f-0.58)/0.42, 0, 1); fade = a*(1 - WG*WG*WG)*clamp((r0 - S0*1.47 - rr)/(S0*0.83), 0, 1). Color: "u" theme 2, "t" accent 1, "e" accent 2, "c" accent 0, "h" and "g" theme 2, "j" theme 1, "H" theme 2, "m" theme 3 times 0.8 alpha, "q" theme 3, "k" theme 3 times 0.62 alpha, "M" accent 5, else theme 1, all with alpha fade; then mix its RGB toward ember (1.0,0.42,0.18) dark or (0.55,0.2,0.1) light by WG*0.8. Weight 1 for "u", "h", "g", "j", "H", else 0. tilt = 0.75+0.25*(1-f). The bands drawn in the crawl (rule, code plate, accent bar, header underline) use alpha times (1 - WG) cubed on top of fade, since only text is pulled into the hole. When fade exceeds 0.01: "r" draws a one-color band rr - size*0.5 to rr - size*0.43 over c ± bw*size/S0*0.8/rr in theme 2 alpha fade*0.35; code and tables keep fixed angles taken at r0 (not rr), so their left edges form one continuous straight edge and indentation and columns line up: "c" with ce = (bw*0.9 + S0*0.6)/r0 first draws a one-color band rr - line height(size) to rr (consecutive code lines tile with no overlap) over c - ce to c + ce in (0.07,0.09,0.14) alpha fade*0.85 when dark or (0.9,0.87,0.8) alpha fade*0.85 when light, then an accent bar band over the same radii from c + ce - 3/r0 to c + ce in accent 0 alpha fade*0.8, then left-aligned arc text of x at L; "b" and "H" are left-aligned arc text of x at L with cw = WRAPU*S0*0.9 over (count of byte 9 in x plus 1), and "H" adds a one-color band rr + size*0.12 to rr + size*0.19 over c ± bw*0.9/r0 in theme 2 alpha fade*0.45; "h" adds the same kind of band rr + size*0.1 to rr + size*0.15 over c ± bw*0.9/r0 in theme 2 alpha fade*0.3 and then left-aligned arc text of x at L; "q" draws a band rr - line height(size) to rr over L - 2.5/r0 to L in theme 2 alpha fade*0.6, then left-aligned arc text of x at L - S0*0.9/r0; "u", "m" and "M" draw centered arc text of the prefix followed by x at c; every other kind with text draws left-aligned arc text of the prefix followed by x at L. The prefix is "→ " for every "t" line, with no condition. For "u" it is "› " and for "e" it is "× ", each only when the line before l (index minus 1) is missing or has a different kind letter, so a wrapped continuation gets none. Every other kind has no prefix. All crawl arc text uses rr, size, the color, weight and tilt; cw is 0 except table rows. rr shrinks by line height(size) times 0.55 when l is just "p", 1.3 for "h" and "g", else 1. Then WG = 0.

The prompt for session i continues the crawl into vb. live means i's platform is available and i is not demo. ps = S0*1.05; track radii ti = r0 - ps*1.4 and to = r0 + ps*0.5; text middle tm = (ti + to)*0.5 - ps*0.1 and prompt text radius tr = arc_mid(tm, c, ps); half angle th = min(hw*0.9, W*0.42/r0) where hw is the sector half width. Draw a one-color band ti to to over c ± th in theme 4 alpha a*0.72 dark or white alpha a*0.75 light; band ti - 1 to ti + 1 theme 2 alpha a*0.55; band to - 1.5 to to + 1.5 theme 2 alpha a*0.9. For live CUR that is busy with empty INPUT: centered arc text status(i) at tr, c, ps, accent 4 alpha a*(0.78 + 0.22*sin(NOW*3)), weight 0, tilt 1, and no caret. For live CUR that is not busy with empty INPUT: centered arc text "› Ask " + platform name + " anything…" at tr, c, ps, theme 3 alpha a*0.8, weight 0, tilt 1, then e = (2c - its end angle) - `sdf_text_w`("› ", ps)/tr. For live CUR with text: centered arc text "› " + INPUT with newlines shown as spaces at tr, c, ps, theme 2 alpha a, weight 1, tilt 1, and e is its end angle. Live CUR, unless busy with empty INPUT, then draws a caret spoke at angle e from tm - ps*0.57 to tm + ps*0.7, width 2.5, theme 2 alpha a*(0.55 + 0.45*cos(NOW*5.5)). Other live sessions draw centered "› " at tr, c, ps, theme 2 alpha a weight 1 tilt 1; sessions that are not live draw centered status(i) at radius arc_mid(tm, c, S0*0.9) and size S0*0.9 in their tone color alpha a, weight 0, tilt 1.

Rim of a sector at c, half width hw, platform q, flags on and busy, into vs: bw = H*0.05; gold (1,0.82,0.45) dark or (0.72,0.52,0.16) light; all bands span c-hw to c+hw. 12 one-color bands R-(k+1)*3 to R-k*3 gold alpha (0.22 dark, 0.12 light)*(1-k/12)*(1-k/12). Bezel: 7 bands k from R+bw*k/7 to R+bw*(k+1)/7 with u = (k+0.5)/7, v = 1 - |2u-1|, color mix of (0.10,0.12,0.17) and (0.27,0.30,0.37) by v*0.8 + 0.2*(1-u) when dark, or of (0.80,0.74,0.62) and (0.97,0.94,0.87) when light, alpha 0.97. Band R+bw*0.58 to R+bw*0.9 platform color alpha 0.33 when on else 0.2. Band R+1 to R+bw*0.22 white alpha 0.07 dark or 0.3 light. Band R-1 to R+1.5 gold alpha 1; band R+bw*0.5-0.5 to R+bw*0.5+0.5 gold 0.25; band R+bw-1 to R+bw+1 gold 0.75. 7 bands R+bw+k*3 to R+bw+(k+1)*3 black alpha (0.35 dark, 0.08 light)*(1-k/7). Sheen: t = NOW, sc = c-hw + (t*0.15 - floor(t*0.15))*2*hw; for k below 15, d = (k-7)/7, a0 = sc + d*0.035, band R to R+bw over a0 to a0+0.0048 color (1,0.97,0.88) alpha 0.22*(1-d*d). Ticks: tk = 0.0087, a from c-hw - (c-hw)%tk while below c+hw stepping tk; big when |a/tk - floor(a/tk/5)*5| is below 0.5; spoke from R+2 to R+bw*0.32 (big) or R+bw*0.2, width 1, gold alpha 0.5 or 0.28. Label: platform name in upper case with a thin space (U+2009) after every letter but the last, then "   ·   ", the rank shown, " / ", cnt(q); size ls = S0*0.62, centered arc text at arc_mid(R + bw*0.5, c, ls), color (1,0.97,0.9) dark or theme 1 light, alpha 1, weight 1, tilt 1; the rank shown is rank(CUR)+1 when on or CUR's platform is q, else 1. When on and CUR's context tokens are above 0, a context meter across the visible part of the rim, with f = CUR's context fraction, hm = min(hw, W*0.4/R) and e = c + hm: a one-color band R + bw*0.8 to R + bw*0.92 over c - hm to e in black alpha 0.35 when dark or 0.12 when light, a band over the same radii from e - f*hm*2 to e in the gauge color for f alpha 0.9, and a disc at pt(R + bw*0.86, e - f*hm*2) of radius 3.5 in the gauge color alpha 1. When busy, a comet: head = c - hw + (NOW*0.23 - floor(NOW*0.23))*2*hw; for k below 14 a disc at pt(R, head - k*0.0035) of radius 3.5*(1-k/14)+0.8, color (1,0.93,0.75) alpha (1-k/14)*(1-k/14).

Platform tab geometry for q: tab width 172, x0 = W - 172 - 24, y = 18 + q*38, height 30, skew 7; the plus zone is the rightmost 30 pixels. Arrow buttons sit at x 44 and W-44, y = H*0.55.

Keycap legend at (x, y) into vs, for pairs ("← →","session"), ("1–4","platform"), ("+","new"), ("Ctrl T","theme"), ("↑ ↓","scroll"), ("Enter","send"): w = `sdf_text_w`(key, 9) + 10; rect (x, y, w, 15) theme 2 alpha 0.45, rect (x+1, y+1, w-2, 13) theme 4 alpha 0.9; flat key at (x+5, y+3.5) size 9 theme 1 alpha 0.9 weight 1; flat label at (x+w+5, y+3.5) size 9 theme 3 alpha 0.85; x grows by w + 5 + label width + 10.

The HUD into vs. Logo vertices copied with each position mapped to (20+20+x*20, 18+20+y*20). Flat "A M N I   D I A L" with every plain space between letters a thin space (U+2009) at (70, 20) size 15 theme 2 alpha 1 weight 1. Status dot: tone of CUR; pulse = 0.55+0.45*sin(NOW*4) when busy else 1; disc at (75, 49) radius 7 tone alpha 0.18*pulse, disc radius 3.5 tone alpha pulse; flat status(CUR) at (85, 44) size 10.5 theme 1 alpha 0.85. Path line at (70, 62) size 9 theme 3 alpha 0.8: tilde form of CUR's cwd, or of its directory when the cwd is empty, shortened when longer than 48 bytes to "…/" plus its last three slash-separated parts, then "  ·  session " and the first 8 bytes of its id when the id is non-empty. Chips: a chip at (x, y) with label l, value v, color k and meter m (negative for none) has lw = `sdf_text_w`(l, 8), vw = `sdf_text_w`(v, 10), w = lw + vw + 22 plus 63 when m is not negative; rect (x, y, w, 19) in k with alpha 0.42, rect (x+1, y+1, w-2, 17) theme 4 alpha 0.92; flat l at (x+7, y+6) size 8 theme 3 alpha 0.85 weight 1; flat v at (x+lw+14, y+4.5) size 10 in k alpha 1 weight 1; with a meter, rect (x+lw+vw+22, y+8, 56, 3.5) theme 3 alpha 0.28 and rect (x+lw+vw+22, y+8, 56*m, 3.5) in k alpha 1; it returns x + w + 7. From x = 70 at y = 77, for CUR: "MODEL" with its model (dropping a leading "claude-") in theme 2 when the model is non-empty; "CONTEXT" with the integer percent of its context fraction, "%  ", compact context tokens, " / " and compact window, in the gauge color, meter at the fraction, when its context tokens are above 0; "SPENT" with "$" + fixed 2 decimals of its cost, then "  ·  " + turns + (" turn" when turns is 1 else " turns") when turns are above 0, then "  ·  " + compact output tokens + " out" when those are above 0, in theme 1, when cost or turns are above 0; "MODE" with its permission mode in accent 1 when non-empty. Legend at (20, 109). Arrow buttons for s 0 and 1 with direction d = -1 then 1 at their spot (ax, ay): for k below 5 a disc radius 30-k*2 theme 2 alpha 0.04; disc 23 theme 2 alpha 0.75; disc 21.5 theme 4 alpha 0.92 dark or 1 light; segments of width 3 theme 2 alpha 1 from (ax+d*4, ay) to (ax-d*4, ay-8) and from (ax+d*4, ay) to (ax-d*4, ay+8). Platform tabs, on when q is CUR's platform, with corners (x0+7, y), (x0+179, y), (x0+172, y+30), (x0, y+30): on draws the flat quad expanded by 1.5 in theme 2 alpha 1 then the quad in theme 2 alpha 0.95; off draws the expanded quad in theme 2 alpha 0.3 then the quad in theme 4 alpha 0.78 dark or 0.96 light. A stripe quad (x0+7, y), (x0+11, y), (x0+4, y+30), (x0, y+30) in platform color alpha 1. Flat q+1 at (x0+16, y+10) size 10.5 weight 1 and the name at (x0+31, y+10) size 10.5 weight 1, both theme 0 alpha 1 when on, else theme 1 alpha 1 when available or 0.45; flat "+" at (x0+152, y+8) size 12 weight 1, theme 0 when on else theme 2. For each k below cnt(q), with j = nth(q, k): a disc at (x0-12-k*10, y+15), radius 3.5 when j is CUR else 2.3, accent 4 alpha 1 when j is busy, else theme 2 alpha 1 when j is CUR, else theme 2 alpha 0.45.

Drawing to texture out: gpu(); geometry; hw = span*0.5*RAD; rb = R - H*0.8; front = 1.5708; spinning when |ROT-ROT1| exceeds 0.01; NH = 0; vertex lists va, vb and vh. For each session: c = ang(center), d = |wrap((c-front)/RAD)|*RAD; skip when d exceeds hw*2.7; plate: 7 bands k from rb + (R-rb)*k/7 to rb + (R-rb)*(k+1)/7 over c ± hw in theme 4 with inner alpha 0.55*k/7 and outer alpha 0.55*(k+1)/7 when dark, or 0.85 times those when light, times 0.7 when not CUR; then a band R - H*0.25 to R with inner color platform alpha 0 and outer platform alpha 0.07; when CUR or spinning with d below hw*2, the crawl and prompt with alpha 1 for CUR else clamp(1-d/(hw*2), 0, 1); the rim into vb with on = CUR and busy = the session is busy; at both edges e = c-hw then c+hw, two bands into vb that glow at the rim and fade toward the hole: rb to R+H*0.05 over e ± 3.5/R with inner theme 2 alpha 0 and outer theme 2 alpha 0.1, then rb to R+H*0.05 over e ± 0.75/R with inner theme 2 alpha 0 and outer theme 2 alpha 0.7. Then the HUD into vh, so it stays crisp outside the lens effects. Then: hole pass 0; `sdf_draw(SC, W, H, va)`; hole pass 1; `sdf_draw(SC, W, H, vb)`; when DARK: post pass into BL[0] from SC and SC mode 0 strength 1, then into BL[k] from BL[k-1] mode 1 for k 1 to 3, then additive post passes mode 2 strength 1 into BL[k-1] from BL[k] for k from 3 down to 1; finally a post pass into out from SC with glo BL[0], mode 3, strength 0.9 when DARK else 0; last `sdf_draw(out, W, H, vh)`.

Update with dt: when NOW times 4 crosses into a new whole number (compare with a stored last tick) refresh all. u = clamp((NOW-T0)/SPIN, 0, 1) in reals; e = 4u³ below 0.5 else 1 - pow(-2u+2, 3)/2; ROT = ROT0 + (ROT1-ROT0)*e. With n = visible(CUR): if n exceeds CUR's shown, SCROLL = min(SCROLL + (n-shown), 7); shown = n; SCROLL becomes SCROLL*exp(-7*dt). Smooth scroll: VIEWT = clamp(VIEWT, 0, max(0, CUR's line count - 1)); VIEWF grows by (VIEWT - VIEWF)*(1 - exp(-14*dt)) and becomes VIEWT when within 0.002 of it; VIEW = int(floor(VIEWF)).

Click at m: for the arrow buttons, if |m.x-ax| and |m.y-ay| are both below 26, step -1 or 1 and stop. For platform tabs, inside x0 to x0+179 and y to y+30 (half-open): in the plus zone (x at least x0+149) make a session of q and go to it, else go to LASTP[q]; stop.

Typing. Typing codepoint cp appends its UTF-8 bytes to INPUT (1 byte below 128, 2 below 2048, 3 below 65536, else 4). Rubbing out pops bytes from INPUT while the last is a continuation byte (128 to 191), then pops one more, when INPUT is not empty. Pasting appends `gfx::clipboard()` to INPUT dropping "\r" and turning "\n" and "\t" into spaces.

Interactive: `gfx::open("Amni Dial", W, H, gfx::WINDOW_RESIZABLE as int)`, else print "no window: " and `gfx::error()` and stop; `gfx::text_input(true)`; last = `gfx::time()`. While `gfx::frame()`: NOW = `gfx::time()`; W and H from `gfx::screen_size()` x and y; ctrl is `gfx::key_down("Left Ctrl")` or `gfx::key_down("Right Ctrl")`. For each ev in `gfx::events()`: when ev.kind is 2 (text) and not ctrl, with c the ev.codepoint as int: with INPUT empty, c from 49 to 52 goes to LASTP[c-49] and 43 makes a new session of CUR's platform and goes there; else c of at least 32 is typed. When ev.kind is 1 (key), ev.down is set and ev.scancode equals `gfx::scancode("Backspace")` as i32, rub out. Then with `gfx::key_pressed(name)`: "Left" and "Right" step -1 and 1; "Up" adds 1 to VIEWT and "Down" subtracts 1, "PageUp" adds 12 and "PageDown" subtracts 12, "End" sets VIEWT = 0 and "Home" sets it to CUR's line count; while "Up" or "Down" is held (`gfx::key_down`) VIEWT also moves by 21*dt in that direction, with dt = NOW - last; "Return" sends; with ctrl, "N" makes a new session of CUR's platform and goes there, "T" toggles DARK and "V" pastes; "Escape" calls `gfx::quit()`. wh = `gfx::mouse_wheel()`; VIEWT grows by wh*2.5 (no rounding, so fine-grained wheels and touchpads scroll smoothly). When `gfx::mouse_pressed(1)` click at `gfx::mouse_pos()`. Update with NOW-last, set last = NOW, draw to `gfx::screen()`. `gfx::close()` at the end.

Shots into dir: `mkdir -p '<dir>/frames'`; open headless W by H, else print "no gpu: " + error and stop; an RGBA8 render target. A shot updates by 1/30, draws and saves "dir/name". Filming n frames: each adds 1/30 to NOW and updates by 1/30; when FRAMES is set it also draws, saves "dir/frames/f" + FR zero-padded to 4 digits + ".png" (that path built with str and append, never format), grows FR by 1 and flushes. If OpenCode is available: for k below 3 use nth(3,k) if k is below cnt(3) else make one; refresh; if it has no lines, CUR = it, INPUT = ask k, send. Asks: "In 7 short lines: what makes a polar UI readable?", "Write a 12 line Helium-style haiku sequence about a spinning dial of agents.", "List 7 terse tips for driving several coding agents at once.". Then up to 240 rounds while any session is busy: refresh all, sleep 500 ms. Then reset all sizes and refresh. cc = nth(1,0); go to cc; ROT = ROT0 = ROT1; T0 = -9; shot "dial-rest.png"; HIDE = min(cc lines, 34); cc shown = visible(cc); SCROLL = 0; film 7; while HIDE is positive decrement it and film 4; film 42; shot "dial-crawl.png"; INPUT = "Refactor the crawl so code blocks keep their indentation"; shot "dial-typing.png"; clear INPUT; VIEWT = 21; film 21; shot "dial-history.png"; VIEWT = 14; film 21; shot "dial-table.png"; VIEWT = 0; film 21. Pinned shots of other sessions: pin to session j means go to j, ROT = ROT0 = ROT1, T0 = -9. When nth(1,1) exists as j: write "1" to "<j dir>/busy", pin to j, refresh j, add 12.3 to NOW, set j's busy start to NOW - 12.3, film 7, shot "dial-busy.png", run `rm -f '<j dir>/busy'` and refresh j. When nth(1,2) exists: pin to it, film 7, shot "dial-format.png", VIEWT = 11, film 21, shot "dial-format-top.png", VIEWT = 0. Pin to cc; go to nth(3,0); film 10; shot "dial-spin.png"; film 21; shot "dial-opencode.png"; step 1, film 28; step 1, film 28; go to LASTP[2], film 28; go to nth(0,0), film 28; go to cc, film 28; DARK off; shot "dial-ivory.png"; DARK on; close.

Main: HOME from env; ROOT is env AMNI_DIAL_HOME when set and non-empty, else HOME + "/.amni-dial". Check availability, scan, call `sdf_system_font()` (system TrueType font with Unicode, before any text is measured), build the logo, measure font metrics. Arguments in order, for each index k: "--send" with two more sets ask = clamp(int of next - 1, 0, 3) and INPUT to the one after; "--dark" sets DARK; "--ivory" clears DARK; "--frames" sets FRAMES; "--seed" with one more seeds from it; "--shots" with one more sets the shots dir. Refresh all; CUR = first Claude session; go to it; ROT = ROT1. With an ask: go to LASTP[ask], send, then up to 480 times while CUR is busy sleep 500 ms and refresh; print each line of CUR without its kind byte. Then shots when a dir is given, else interactive when there is no ask.
